    "updated_at": "2025-01-21T09:55:14Z",
    "body": "And I don't think this applies in this case. Saying you shouldn't use `X-Frame-Options` is dangerous and unhelpful.\n\nIf you want to use `ALLOW-FRAME` then you have to use CSP's `frame-ancestors` directive and that **IS** a \"Do not use\" use case for `X-Frame-Options`, but for the basic `DENY` or `SAMEORIGIN` use case `X-Frame-Options` is fine, and is not going anywhere. And arguably it is better than spending effort implementing an equivalent CSP with only a `frame-ancestors`'s directive that makes it look like you have a CSP, when you haven't added any benefit.\n\nThis can be seen at OWASP's guidance for example: https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Clickjacking_Defense_Cheat_Sheet.html.\n\nCC: @mikewest @arturjanc @terjanq",
